A||N||3||MikeSchaefer||A New Stance for the Beast....||||5||
Z||000000||MikeSchaefer||03-28-2001||08:25 PM||||Hey Dudes & Dudets,<BR>Fiero Bob is taking my car to get two stock 85 GT springs put on the rear this weekend, it was 2" lowered all the way around previously.  I am thinking this will be a cool-ass stance and help with weight distribution, anyone tried this?  I mentioned it a while ago so I guess I'm just following up, I'll have pics next week I hope.<BR>BTW It's getting an alignment so I won't die,<BR>Mike Schaefer <A HREF="http://surf.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://surf.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||03-29-2001||12:57 AM||||Are the 85 GT springs going to be cut or are you going to have the stock height in the back? The Fiero might have a little more tendency to come around on you if the back is higher...But it will have a nice stance. I went down 2 inches in front and 1 1/2 in the back. With 16 inch wheels its very nice! Its not very noticeable except for certain angles. Not to mention a possible tendency to bottom out the front end on quick stops!<P>Stock weight distribution was 49/51. Maybe it would or maybe it would over compensate!||||reg||14
Z||000002||MikeSchaefer||03-29-2001||03:15 AM||||Yeah I'm going to be keeping them stock.  AHH, I didn't know that stock distro was 49/51, that's really good.  I thought it was more like 40/60.  I hope this doesn't create an offset weight distribution, I guess I'll know on Saturday.  I have 15" rims and big tires, so it should look good.  Do you have any pics of your car?  I'd like to see that.<BR>Later,<BR>Mike||||reg||4
Z||000003||pontiacs4me||03-29-2001||04:22 AM||||I read that the weight distribution was 43/57, I guess it depends on what engine you have.||||reg||1
